Night Owl
Original: https://github.com/sdras/night-owl-vscode-theme
Commit: cc291eba7976b20d7c66bde6883c27b902196b07
Source: themes/Night Owl-color-theme.json
Git blob: 729b426531cb574f5d9c8dd425209c83a8103056
MIT; see NIGHT-OWL-LICENSE for the original copyright notice.

All three JSON snapshots retain upstream values. community-themes.ts filters
non-string/null workbench entries, supplies missing UI/reader roles from the
same palette, and maps lexical/LSP/Prism roles to the ordered token rules.
Full TextMate selectors are retained for the existing Shiki grammar engine.
For Setdown's existing >=4.5:1 editor/notebook comment contrast guarantee,
Night Owl's #637777 becomes #7c9090 and Dracula's #6272A4 becomes #8293bf
in token rules only. Original terminal ANSI colors are retained; xterm keeps
its existing 4.5 minimum contrast correction. No upstream default/settings
code is imported. These adaptations preserve the document layout and fonts.
Fenced reader code uses each theme's editor background so its syntax colors
retain the same contrast as source editing.

