Copyright (c) 2015 Mahmoud Ali. MIT; see ATOM-ONE-LIGHT-LICENSE.
The JSON is formatted without changing source values.

The light imports use light Monaco/Shiki defaults and the GitHub Light
reader base, preserving document layout and fonts. Light Owl's #989fb1 becomes
#6a7181 and Atom One Light's #A0A1A7 becomes #696c77 in token rules only to
retain the existing >=4.5:1 comment contrast guarantee. The original JSON
snapshots retain those source colors. Atom's legacy token value "white" maps
to #ffffff and "inherit" is omitted in the runtime adapter. Atom supplies no
terminal ANSI overrides, so it uses VS Code's light ANSI defaults with the
existing xterm minimum contrast correction. No extension code is executed.
